---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout current="Knowledge" title="Knowledge Library" description="A working library of resources, questions, research directions and ideas to build.">
  <div class="eyebrow">A PERSONAL KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM</div>
  <h1>Knowledge Library</h1>
  <p class="lede">A place to connect what I read, what I think, what I want to investigate and what I might build.</p>
  <div class="prose intro">
    <p>Knowledge becomes more useful when it leaves a trace. A book should lead to a question. A paper should suggest an experiment. An idea should eventually meet reality.</p>
    <p>This library is a working map, not a list of accomplishments. Some entries are starting points; others will become notes, hypotheses, prototypes or research projects.</p>
  </div>
  <section class="knowledge-section">
    <div class="section-index">01 / READ</div><div class="section-content">
      <h2>Read</h2><p>Books, essays, courses, lectures and papers worth spending time with. The goal is not to collect links, but to understand the ideas behind them.</p>
      <div class="resource"><a href="https://guzey.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alexey Guzey — Essays, research and notes ↗</a><p>A broad collection spanning science, technology, research, education and progress.</p></div>
      <div class="resource"><a href="https://guzey.com/tools-gear/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alexey Guzey — Tools / Gear ↗</a><p>A personal inventory of tools, software and equipment, with reflections on how they support work and learning. The author notes that the recommendations are outdated, so use it as inspiration rather than a current buying guide.</p></div>
      <div class="resource"><a href="https://cba.mit.edu/classes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT Center for Bits and Atoms — Classes ↗</a><p>Course materials connected to digital fabrication, computation and the relationship between bits and atoms.</p></div>
      <div class="resource"><a href="https://andzuck.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Andrej Karpathy — Website and writing ↗</a><p>A starting point for exploring ideas around technology, intelligence and learning.</p></div>
      <div class="resource"><a href="https://www.squibler.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Squibler — AI-assisted writing ↗</a><p>A writing workspace for developing ideas into structured drafts, books, novels and screenplays, with AI support for outlining and editing.</p></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/reading/">Open reading notes →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="knowledge-section">
    <div class="section-index">02 / THINK</div><div class="section-content">
      <h2>Think</h2><p>Questions, observations, arguments and hypotheses that deserve more thought. These are not conclusions; they are ideas to examine and improve.</p>
      <ul><li>What makes a complex system understandable?</li><li>How can scientific knowledge become practical engineering capability?</li><li>What conditions allow a small research laboratory to produce useful breakthroughs?</li><li>Can beautiful design and technical efficiency reinforce one another?</li></ul>
      <a class="text-link" href="/questions/">Explore open questions →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="knowledge-section">
    <div class="section-index">03 / RESEARCH</div><div class="section-content">
      <h2>Research</h2><p>Topics to investigate through papers, technical literature, calculations and experiments. Each research note should state the question, evidence, methods, limitations and next steps.</p>
      <div class="topic-list"><span>Materials science</span><span>Coatings & corrosion</span><span>Mechanical design</span><span>Advanced manufacturing</span><span>Robotics</span><span>Control systems</span><span>Industrial systems</span></div>
      <p class="small-note">A research direction becomes stronger when it can be expressed as a precise question that evidence could answer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="knowledge-section">
    <div class="section-index">04 / BUILD</div><div class="section-content">
      <h2>Build</h2><p>Ideas that could become models, prototypes, tools, experiments or useful systems. Building is a way to test whether an idea survives contact with reality.</p>
      <div class="resource"><strong>Robotics & Innovation Laboratory</strong><p>Explore what a practical research and experimentation space could look like: equipment, capabilities, projects, collaborators and a path from learning to making.</p></div>
      <div class="resource"><strong>Industrial Engineering Lab</strong><p>Turn industrial problems into measurable improvements through diagnosis, design, maintenance and process understanding.</p></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See projects in progress →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="closing-note"><strong>A simple rule</strong><p>For every important thing I read, try to leave one useful trace: a summary, a question, a connection, an experiment or an idea worth testing.</p></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.intro{max-width:720px;margin:28px 0 54px}.knowledge-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px minmax(0,1fr);gap:34px;padding:30px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.section-index{font:10px 'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--muted);padding-top:9px}.section-content{max-width:690px}.section-content h2{font:30px 'Literata',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;margin:0 0 10px}.section-content>p{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 20px}.resource{padding:15px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.resource a,.resource strong{font:16px 'Literata',Georgia,serif;color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none}.resource a:hover{color:var(--accent)}.resource p{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin:6px 0 0}.section-content ul{padding-left:19px;color:var(--ink);font-size:14px;line-height:2}.topic-list{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:18px 0}.topic-list span{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:7px 10px;font:10px 'DM Mono',monospace;color:var(--muted)}.small-note{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.closing-note{margin:35px 0 10px;padding:22px 24px;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);background:#f3f0e9;max-width:720px}.closing-note strong{font:17px 'Literata',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}.closing-note p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted);margin:7px 0 0}@media(max-width:600px){.knowledge-section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px;padding:24px 0}.section-index{padding:0}.section-content h2{font-size:27px}}
</style>